.TH "BLOB.STREAM" "3JS" "September 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Blob.stream \- Blob: stream() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]stream()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]Blob\f[R]
interface returns a \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] which upon reading returns
the data contained within the \f[CR]Blob\f[R] as chunks of raw bytes.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
stream()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] which, upon reading, returns the contents of
the \f[CR]Blob\f[R].
.SH USAGE NOTES
With \f[CR]stream()\f[R] and the returned \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R], you
gain several interesting capabilities:
.IP \(bu 2
Call \f[CR]getReader()\f[R] on the returned stream to get an object to
use to read the data from the blob using methods such as the
\f[CR]ReadableStreamDefaultReader\f[R] interface\(cqs \f[CR]read()\f[R]
method.
.IP \(bu 2
Call the returned stream\(cqs \f[CR]pipeTo()\f[R] method to pipe the
blob\(cqs data to a writable stream.
.IP \(bu 2
Call the returned stream\(cqs \f[CR]tee()\f[R] method to \f[B]tee\f[R]
the readable stream.
This returns an array containing two new \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R]
objects, each of which returns the contents of the \f[CR]Blob\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
Call the returned stream\(cqs \f[CR]pipeThrough()\f[R] method to pipe
the stream through a \f[CR]TransformStream\f[R] or any other readable
and writable pair.
> \f[B]Note:\f[R] > \f[CR]Blob.textStream()\f[R] is a useful shortcut
that immediately returns a \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] of UTF\-8 text
chunks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Response.body\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Streams API
